---
import { LIMITS } from '@lib/solutions/self-hosting';
---

<section class="border-t border-line" aria-labelledby="sh-limits-title">
  <div class="wrap py-16 md:py-24 grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10 lg:gap-12">
    <div class="lg:col-span-5">
      <h2 id="sh-limits-title" class="h2">
        The free plan’s limits are two environment settings.
      </h2>
      <p class="prose mt-5 max-w-[46ch]">
        A plan is a limit preset and nothing more: no billing code, no feature gating. On your own install, these two
        variables replace the free plan’s numbers without touching the code. Each takes a positive whole number.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="lg:col-span-6 lg:col-start-7">
      <ul class="panel sh-limits">
        {LIMITS.map(limit => (
          <li class="panel-pad">
            <p class="sh-var">
              <code>{limit.name}</code>
              <span class="sh-default">Default: {limit.fallback}</span>
            </p>
            <p class="prose mt-3 text-base">{limit.effect}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-fg-2">
        Per-file and rate limits stay as they are: 100 MB a file, 50 attachments an issue, and API rate limits returned
        in response headers.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .sh-limits > li + li {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .sh-var {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 6px 14px;
  }
  .sh-var code {
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text);
    background: var(--bg-inset);
    padding: 2px 8px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-xs);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .sh-default {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
</style>
